(Outcome O1: distinguish a requirement, evidence and an assumption.) Tj
T*
(An engineering brief states what a solution must achieve, the limits it must respect) Tj
T*
(and how success will be checked. A requirement is testable; an assumption is a) Tj
T*
(condition taken as true until checked. A measurement is useful evidence only when its) Tj
T*
(method, units and limits are known.) Tj
T*
(Classroom case: a model-aircraft storage rack must hold six models within a supplied) Tj
T*
(floor-space limit. 'Looks strong' is not an acceptance criterion. 'Supports the stated) Tj
T*
(classroom load without permanent deformation in the specified test' identifies a) Tj
T*
(measurable outcome, but the instructor must define the load, setup and limits.) Tj
T*
(Record the document title, revision and source before using a table. Conflicting) Tj
T*
(versions require clarification rather than silent mixing.) Tj
